 r←EscapeAttributeValue text
⍝ Escapes `text` for use as the value of an HTML attribute written in double quotes.
⍝ `EscapeSpecialChars` sees to &, < and > but not to the double quote, which would end the
⍝ attribute early and turn whatever follows into markup of its own. That matters here
⍝ because the text comes from a package config, so it is written by somebody else.
⍝ The order is not arbitrary: & is escaped first, by `EscapeSpecialChars`, so the & of the
⍝ "&quot;" put in afterwards is not escaped a second time.
 r←'"'⎕R'\&quot;'⊣EscapeSpecialChars text            ⍝ \& because a bare & means the whole match
⍝Done
